  "scope": "Interchangeable one-per-region navigation and onboard radio with shared integral support; existing optical models and independent servo module preserved.",
  "intentional_changes": [
    "Add source-selected P-AS, MG-A01 (M10 Ultra) and bare MG-F10-A navigation profiles, plus LR900-A and LR24-F-Mini onboard radio profiles. Preserve the default selections. LR24-F is ground equipment.",
    "Extend the common navigation member to the GPS pad at carrier (100, 0) mm. The continuous 14 x 3 mm member and 18 x 18 mm adhesive pad add no printed part or fastener. Both optical hosts clear the conservative direct-helix envelope.",
    "Move the shared radio pad and its installed body/end reservations 3 mm along carrier Y to centre Y=50 mm. The wider Mini must preserve the existing 2 mm FC wiring-reservation gap.",
    "Check six mutually exclusive navigation/radio combinations against both optical sensors and both hosts, continuous field bounds, connector allowances, adhesive plan overlap and service. Exact port datums, rear contact and retention remain unqualified.",
    "Permit direct and remote MG-F10 SMA arrangements. Direct +Z points downward and establishes mechanical clearance only. The remote upward antenna position, support and extension remain unmodeled. MG-A01 sky view is also unqualified.",
    "The known default equipment subtotal changes from 33.032 to 37.032 g by including the manufacturer's LR900-A 4 g reference. This is not a physical mass increase. The selected MG-F10 body (6 g) and helix (15 g) are counted separately, once each. Connector, power and ground-radio differences remain explicit."
  ],
